course: dictionary
lesson: 5534
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word «left» has more than one meaning, so you need the context to know which one the writer means. Read the words around it. «Two cakes are left» means two are still there after the others have gone.
explain: «Left» can also be the past of leave, meaning went away from a place. «She left the room at nine o'clock» tells you she went out of the room. Try the swap test: put «went away from» into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: «Left» can also be a side, the opposite of right. «Turn left at the big tree» is a direction. Look at the other words: a map, a turn or a side tells you that this is the meaning you need.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Left» can mean still remaining: «one biscuit left» means one biscuit is still there.
fact: «Left» is the past of leave: «He left» means he went away.
fact: «Left» is also a side, the opposite of right. «Left behind» means not taken along, and «leftovers» is food that was not eaten.
fact: «He left us» can gently mean someone has died, so always read the whole text to be sure.
exercise: «Two cakes are left on the plate.» How many cakes are still on the plate? | *Two | None at all | Ten | Five
exercise: «She left the room at nine o'clock.» What does left mean here? | *Went out of | Cleaned | Sold | Stayed inside
exercise: Mum says, «Turn ___ at the big tree.» Which word fits the gap? | leave | lift | *left | leaving
test: «The actors were left stuck on stage when one of them forgot his lines.» What does left mean here? | Were lucky | *Remained, still stuck there | Danced | Went home happily
test: «The heart is tipped a little to the left in the middle of the chest.» What does left mean here? | Leftover food | Still there, like one biscuit | *A side of the body | Gone away
exam: «Five apples are left in the bowl.» Which formal word could replace left without changing the meaning? | carried | *remaining | departed from | lifted
